% Olex2's references: every work Olex2 cites, defined once.
%
% Read by util/pyUtil/PyToolLib/References.py; the CIF text (IUCr style), the
% short form "(Sheldrick, 2015)" and the recognition of a work in an existing
% CIF all come from these fields.  Plain BibTeX, so the file also opens in a
% reference manager.
%
% author   "Surname, I. and Surname, I.", "and others" for et al.; accents as
%          CIF codes in braces: Pr{\'o}chniak
% volume   as printed: A71 for Acta Cryst. A
% doi      checked against Crossref (2026-11-19); a work without one has none
% markers  only where the default recognition is not enough.  By default a
%          work is recognised in CIF text by its DOI, or by first author +
%          year + volume and pages.  Groups separated by '|', the items of a
%          group (all must occur) by ';'; letters and digits only are compared.
% note     'in press' prints instead of volume and pages
% programs names a _computing_* item may give for the program this work is
%          cited for, ';' between names: whole words, any case, the longest
%          name wins ('SHELXL-97' is not also 'SHELXL'); read by
%          References.for_software()

